greet: the first wizard, declared in residency and packed into the control bottle

## What this is

The first wizard, named `greet`: meeting someone at the `you` subdomain. Onboarding — staff or client; bind a
first passkey here, then open what is sealed to it. It is what the control bottle already walked
people through; now it has a name, a declaration, and a place.

- `wizards/greet/` — `NAME`, `README.md` (the onboarding; steps are sub-resources it employs),
  `CONSTITUTION.md` (clubhouse rules, shouty), `_data/control.yml`. Moved from `control/`, which
  was this wizard without knowing it.
- `residency.yml` — `.you-engine` now declares one wizard under `wizards:`, referenced by **label**
  and never by pin, with `workflow: [bind-key, open-sealed, read]` namespaced under it. `wants: []`,
  `serves: []` — a control point publishes and guides, nothing to store or run.
- `bin/control init [wizard]` packs `wizards/<name>/` (default `greet`) into the orphan control
  branch, so the bottle that ships IS the wizard.

## Merge qualifications

- [x] the wizard has a label, an entry README, and a constitution beside it
- [x] residency declares it by label with no version, per library#wizards/residency-declares-them
- [x] `bin/control init` + `bin/publish` round-trip; `bin/test` green (gif, bottle, reader, sealed)
- [x] the control branch republished and bottled from `wizards/greet/`
- [ ] station-node rolls `.you-engine` — it becomes `claimed` (has a residency.yml) instead of `quiet`
- [ ] the workflow labels get their mapping (bind-key, open-sealed, read → what each permits)
- [ ] a second wizard exists, proving the namespace holds
